## fix(mapping-ui): wire Designer "Unmap all" via addEventListener for reliable confirm popup

**Context:** Follow-up to the "Unmap all" work below. The Designer button was wired with an inline `onclick="confirmResetMappings()"`, which reintroduced the inline-handler pattern the team deliberately dropped in v0.2.0 (in favor of id-based `addEventListener`). Switched it to the same robust wiring as the Information button so the confirmation dialog (`showConfirmDialog`) fires reliably before any mappings are cleared.

**Changes:**
1. `src/front/templates/partials/mapping/_mapping_design.html` — Removed the inline `onclick="confirmResetMappings()"` from `#resetMappingsDesignBtn` (kept the id).
2. `src/front/static/global/js/mapping-information.js` — `_initMappingInformationButtons()` now wires both `#resetMappingsBtn` and `#resetMappingsDesignBtn` to `confirmResetMappings()` via `addEventListener` with the existing `obResetWired` de-dup guard.

**Modified files:**
- `src/front/templates/partials/mapping/_mapping_design.html`
- `src/front/static/global/js/mapping-information.js`

**Test result:** UI-only change (no automated JS coverage); full backend suite green (3320 passed, 275 skipped).

